Third-party components and data
-------------------------------
The software includes third-party software, type and data — open-source libraries, the Lora typeface, word meanings
adapted from English Wiktionary, Tatoeba and Universal Dependencies sentences, UniMorph, OpenRussian, verbecc,
Morfologik and frequency-list data, and a TypeScript port of py-fsrs — that remain under their own licences. They are
listed, with their licence texts and the credits they require, in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md (also served by the app at
/third-party-notices.txt and summarised at /notices) and in docs/FREQUENCY_SETS.md. Those licences govern their
use, and nothing in this notice restricts the rights they grant.

